    "body": "So this is a fun one.\r\n\r\nConventionally in Arch, the `$` sign is used for regular user prompts, while the `#` sign is used for superuser prompts.\r\n\r\nSo we can do `# yay -S starship` or `$ sudo yay -S starship` but probably not `$` without sudo.",
